{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the sum of all pairwise differences of outcomes between the two lotteries. To compute this, we compare each outcome of Lottery A with each outcome of Lottery B. The outcomes are: A: -3000 (0.2%), 0 (99.8%); B: -6000 (0.1%), 0 (99.9%). The pairwise outcome differences are: (-3000) - (-6000) = +3000; (-3000) - 0 = -3000; 0 - (-6000) = +6000; 0 - 0 = 0. The sum of these differences is 3000 - 3000 + 6000 + 0 = 6000. Since the sum is positive, the reason would favor Lottery A (as it has the more favorable sum of outcome differences). The relevant information (the outcomes) is available in the lotteries, so the reason can be applied.",
